-w=\"7\">does</span> <span data-s=\"79\" data-w=\"8\">on</span> <span data-s=\"79\" data-w=\"9\">the</span> <span data-s=\"79\" data-w=\"10\">data</span> <span data-s=\"79\" data-w=\"11\">it</span> <span data-s=\"79\" data-w=\"12\">was</span> <span data-s=\"79\" data-w=\"13\">trained</span> <span data-s=\"79\" data-w=\"14\">on</span> <span data-s=\"79\" data-w=\"15\">(Chapter</span> <span data-s=\"79\" data-w=\"16\">3).</span></li>\n<li><span data-s=\"80\" data-w=\"0\">Spending</span> <span data-s=\"80\" data-w=\"1\">weeks</span> <span data-s=\"80\" data-w=\"2\">on</span> <span data-s=\"80\" data-w=\"3\">the</span> <span data-s=\"80\" data-w=\"4\">algorithm</span> <span data-s=\"80\" data-w=\"5\">when</span> <span data-s=\"80\" data-w=\"6\">the</span> <span data-s=\"80\" data-w=\"7\">data</span> <span data-s=\"80\" data-w=\"8\">is</span> <span data-s=\"80\" data-w=\"9\">wrong.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Check yourself</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Explain the difference between a rule-based system and a machine learning system, using a loan example.</li>\n<li>Name the two phases of a model's life and say which one is expensive.</li>\n<li>Is deep learning a way to learn, like supervised learning? Explain.</li>\n<li>Give one task in a bank where you would write a rule instead of training a model.</li>\n</ul>\n<details class=\"answers\"><summary>Show answers</summary><p> (1) A rule-based system applies rules a person wrote; a learning system finds the pattern from past files and their outcomes. (2) Training and inference; training is the expensive one. (3) No. It is a type of model that can be trained in any of the three ways. (4) For example checking that an applicant is of legal age.</p></details>\n<p><strong>Go deeper:</strong> <a href=\"https://developers.google.com/machine-learning/crash-course\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Machine Learning Crash Course</a> (Google, free) · Pedro Domingos, <a href=\"https://homes.cs.washington.edu/~pedrod/papers/cacm12.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">A Few Useful Things to Know about Machine Learning</a> (short, practical, readable) · the videos behind this chapter: <a class=\"vlink\" href=\"#/watch/BUTjcAjfMgY\">ML Foundations for AI Engineers</a> (Shaw Talebi) and Ng, course 1, videos 1 to 3.</p>\n"}